ef 17592186387460 13194139536177 true] [17592186119777 1020 #edb/ref 17592186387467 13194139536177 true] [17592186120443 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536177 true] [17592186120443 1100 "Find the values of $k$ such that the vector $b$ lies in $Span{a_{1}, a_{2}}$, where\n\n$a_{1} = \\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}, a_{2} = \\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 18\\end{bmatrix}, b = \\begin{bmatrix}-12 \\\\ -10 \\\\ k\\end{bmatrix}$." 13194139536177 false] [17592186120443 1100 "Find the values of $k$ such that the vector $b$ lies in $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 18\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-12 \\\\ -10 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139536177 true] [17592186120443 1145 "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 18\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-12 \\\\ -10 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-3{x}_{1}+9{x}_{2}=-12 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+7{x}_{2}=-10 \\\\ -6{x}_{1}+18{x}_{2}=k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}-3 & 9 & -12 \\\\ -2 & 7 & -10 \\\\ -6 & 18 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=-\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 7 & -10 \\\\ -6 & 18 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -6 & 18 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+6{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k+24\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=k+24.$ Therefore, the system has a solution only if\n\n$$\n0=k+24\\,⇒\\,k=-24.\n$$" 13194139536177 true] [17592186387411 1017 #edb/ref 17592186387412 13194139536177 true] [17592186387411 1089 "q-105248" 13194139536177 true] [17592186387411 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536177 true] [17592186387411 1100 "Determine if the vector $u$ lies on the plane $Π:r=sb+tc$, $t,s\\in R$, where  $b=⟨1,-4,2⟩$, $c=⟨3,-10,2⟩$, and  $u=⟨-2,5,0⟩.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of $s\\cdot t$ from the decomposition $u=sb+tc.$" 13194139536177 true] [17592186387411 1113 #uuid "da64bb93-914e-5229-bb6d-b7d97e6fa1bb" 13194139536177 true] [17592186387411 1145 "By definition, $u\\in Π$ if there exist $t$ and $s$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc & =u \\\\ s[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}s+3t=-2 \\\\ -4s-10t=5 \\\\ 2s+2t=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ -4 & -10 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=-2,$ which has no solution.\n\nSo, there are no values of $s$ and $t$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc=u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $u$ does *not* lie on the plane $Π.$" 13194139536177 true] [17592186387412 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387413 13194139536177 true] [17592186387412 1000 #edb/